  - House:Hollis:Kitchen
  greetings:
  - Come in out of the dark, Detective, before it notices you.
  - Harlan's in the field. He's always in the field.
  aboutSelf: Forty years married to Harlan. I keep the house, I keep the hymns, and I keep my gloves on. Eczema. Don't ask to see.
  aboutTown: Folks like to say Semblance is cursed. It isn't. It's chosen. There's a difference, and the difference is you don't get a say.
  seenAnythingStrange: The corn's growing in rows that were never planted. New rows, straight as a ruler, right up to our back door.
  foundersDay: It rained and we sang in the church hall. Mae's cherry pie won. Father Crane preached on the wheat and the tares, and I cried. I don't know why.
  gossip:
  - title: About Mae Whitlock
    response: Mae's burns cover the right side of her face. The fryer, in '70. She went back to work the next week.
  - title: About Hank Marsh
    response: Hank's got an anchor tattooed on the back of his right hand. Navy. June hates it.
